# Tests — MSA Schedule 4 chronic failure

Assertion-based tests for `Chronic_failure`. L-6.1's two triggers are
independent, so they are tested independently as well as together:

  * three consecutive failing periods, and the two-in-a-row case that is one
    short of it, and the case where a single good month breaks the run;
  * four failing periods inside a rolling twelve-month window, with a pattern
    that satisfies this trigger while never producing three in a row, and the
    same four failures spread just too wide to fit any twelve-month window;
  * the rolling window itself at exactly twelve months and at thirteen.

"Less than 99.90%" is tested at exactly 99.90% (not a failure, and it breaks a
run) and at 99.89%. L-6.2's 30-day exercise window is tested at day 30 and day
31, both where notice has been given and where it has not, and the case where
no right ever arose is tested with a far-future assessment date: a right that
does not exist cannot lapse.

L-6.2's window has two ends and lapses per occurrence, so both are tested in
their own right. The `CE0007_` tests put two occurrences fifteen months apart
in one history and require the lapse of the first to leave the second intact.
The `CE0008_` tests put the notice outside the window at the lower end —
dated before the third failing period had even ended, so before any right
existed — and require that it does not exercise anything.

> Using ChronicFailure

## Helper

A Measurement Period is a calendar month, identified by its first and last
day. This constructor keeps the histories below readable; it encodes nothing.

```catala
declaration mp
  content ChronicFailure.PeriodAvailability
  depends on
    starts content date,
    ends content date,
    pct content decimal
  equals
    ChronicFailure.PeriodAvailability {
      -- period_start: starts
      -- period_end: ends
      -- availability_percentage: pct
    }
```

## L6_1_ThreeConsecutive

L-6.1 first trigger: three consecutive Measurement Periods below 99.90%. The
right arises, the completing period is the third of the three, and the second
trigger is not satisfied because there are only three failures in all.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_ThreeConsecutive:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_ThreeConsecutive:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 3
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = true
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = true
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Present content |2025-03-31|
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Present content |2025-04-30|
  assertion r.notice_period_days = 30
  assertion r.early_termination_charges_payable = false
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = true
```

## L6_1_TwoConsecutiveOnly

L-6.1: two consecutive failures are not three. Neither trigger is satisfied,
so no right arises and there is no deadline to compute.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_TwoConsecutiveOnly:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_TwoConsecutiveOnly:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.95
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Absent
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = false
```

## L6_1_GapResetsTheRun

L-6.1: "each of three consecutive Measurement Periods". One good month between
failures breaks the run, and three failures are not four, so neither trigger
fires.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_GapResetsTheRun:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_GapResetsTheRun:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.95;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-04-01|, |2025-04-30|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-05-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-05-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 3
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
```

## L6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineIsNotAFailure

L-6.1 requires the Availability Percentage to be "less than 99.90%", which is
strict and matches L-3.1. Three months at exactly 99.90% are three months in
which the Service Level was met.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineIsNotAFailure:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineIsNotAFailure:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.90;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.90;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.90
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 0
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
```

