## L6_2_NoRightCannotLapse

L-6.2 lapses "the right in L-6.1". Where no right ever arose there is nothing
to lapse, however long ago the history ended — the lapse rule repeats
`right_arisen` from its parent rather than inheriting it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_2_NoRightCannotLapse:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_2_NoRightCannotLapse:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.99
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2030-01-01|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2030-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Absent
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = false
```

